WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:20.000
🎵

00:20.000 --> 00:32.000
🎵

00:32.000 --> 00:40.000
Who steals my purse, steals trash, but he that soils the honor of my nose, that man must grist death by my sword!

00:40.000 --> 00:41.000
I'm gone!

00:43.000 --> 00:45.000
What'd you do that for? It's just getting exciting!

00:45.000 --> 00:47.000
Meyer, it's three o'clock in the morning, I've got to get up early!

00:47.000 --> 00:49.000
But I want to know how the picture ends!

00:49.000 --> 00:51.000
Meyer, it'll be on again, you'll see it then!

00:51.000 --> 00:52.000
I may miss it!

00:52.000 --> 00:54.000
Look, if I tell you how it ends, will you go to sleep?

00:54.000 --> 00:55.000
Well, sure!

00:55.000 --> 00:59.000
Alright, now this picture is all about a fella by the name of Macaruno.

00:59.000 --> 01:04.000
He's a famous poet, he's got a very long nose, and he's a famous saucepan.

01:04.000 --> 01:17.000
🎵

01:17.000 --> 01:21.000
Ah, my dear friend, did you see her by beautiful rock salt?

01:21.000 --> 01:23.000
Indeed I did!

01:23.000 --> 01:26.000
And now I understand why your heart is aflame.

01:26.000 --> 01:30.000
But tell me, why does she hide her wondrous beauty behind a veil?

01:30.000 --> 01:38.000
It is a legend that her face is so beautiful that she veils it so that no one can gaze upon it, except the man that wins her.

01:38.000 --> 01:46.000
Aye, and all the dreamers in the universe cannot conjure up the vision of loveliness that awaits her heaven-appointed husband.

01:46.000 --> 01:50.000
Ah, friend, wouldst that I had thy golden poetic tongue.

01:50.000 --> 01:53.000
🎵

01:53.000 --> 01:55.000
We can't have everything.

01:55.000 --> 01:57.000
Dear friend, please help me win her.

01:57.000 --> 02:01.000
I cannot shape my words to express my soul.

02:01.000 --> 02:05.000
If you would woo the lady rock salt, I am at your service.

02:05.000 --> 02:07.000
Out of the way, peasants!

02:07.000 --> 02:11.000
I have come to woo the lady rock salt.

02:11.000 --> 02:14.000
Peasants? How dare you, sir!

02:14.000 --> 02:18.000
Do not try to detain me, sir, after all a lady is waiting.

02:18.000 --> 02:23.000
Besides, I would not demean myself by doing battle with a creature like you.

02:23.000 --> 02:25.000
Hold your tongue, sir!

02:25.000 --> 02:31.000
You insult my good friend Myrono, and to insult him is to insult me.

02:31.000 --> 02:33.000
Indeed.

02:33.000 --> 02:40.000
Tell me, sir, is that your nose, or are you eating a rather large cucumber?

02:40.000 --> 02:45.000
He insulted my nose, sir.

02:45.000 --> 02:47.000
You should have never made that remark.

02:47.000 --> 02:51.000
Nearly, but how can one ignore such a magnificent nose?

02:51.000 --> 02:56.000
Fill it with gunpowder, and you could blow up half of Paris.

02:56.000 --> 03:02.000
An unfortunate choice of words, sir. Stand back, Myrono.

03:02.000 --> 03:07.000
Dear me, what a bore. Why does everyone want to challenge me?

03:07.000 --> 03:10.000
The consequence.

03:10.000 --> 03:14.000
The consequence? The greatest swordsman in all of Marseille?

03:14.000 --> 03:18.000
Well, I'm afraid my reputation has preceded me to Paris.

03:18.000 --> 03:22.000
You're not going to let him treat you like this, you, the greatest swordsman in all of Paris?

03:22.000 --> 03:26.000
Macaruno the Great, at last we meet.

03:26.000 --> 03:29.000
I have read your poetry, sir.

03:29.000 --> 03:31.000
Oh!

03:31.000 --> 03:34.000
I find it as detestable as your nose.

03:34.000 --> 03:39.000
That's as much as I can take. I challenge you to a duel.

03:39.000 --> 03:45.000
Really, sir, that is no proper way to challenge.

03:45.000 --> 03:50.000
Let me show you. Allow me. Now.

03:54.000 --> 04:00.000
And now, if you'll excuse me, I have a very important engagement with the lady.

04:00.000 --> 04:04.000
Remember, tomorrow night at the Cave of the Bats.

04:04.000 --> 04:07.000
Tavern!

04:07.000 --> 04:12.000
Well, Myrono, I have waited long enough for him to show up. Let us leave.

04:12.000 --> 04:16.000
Macaruno, if you leave now, you lose your honor.

04:16.000 --> 04:20.000
My honor? I am not that much afraid of him.

04:20.000 --> 04:23.000
Ah!

04:23.000 --> 04:26.000
Ah!

04:28.000 --> 04:34.000
I, uh, I may as well warn you, I have had 140 duels and won them all.

04:34.000 --> 04:40.000
And I have had 500 and won them all.

04:40.000 --> 04:44.000
I think the best thing for me to do is to withdraw.

04:44.000 --> 04:50.000
Just because he has had 500 duels and won them all, you don't want to show him you're a coward?

04:50.000 --> 04:53.000
You don't want him to know that you have a yellow streak down your back?

04:53.000 --> 04:55.000
Of course not.

04:55.000 --> 04:57.000
If you leave now, you'll lose your honor.

04:57.000 --> 04:59.000
That's a good idea.

04:59.000 --> 05:01.000
What's a good idea?

05:01.000 --> 05:03.000
Let me lose my honor.

05:03.000 --> 05:07.000
You can't. Besides, he insulted your nose.

05:07.000 --> 05:14.000
He is right. I pointed out that your proboscis is much like a log full of knots.

05:14.000 --> 05:20.000
Well, sticks and stones may break my bones, but they never harm a man.

05:23.000 --> 05:25.000
Who is that?

05:25.000 --> 05:28.000
That must be the doctor.

05:28.000 --> 05:30.000
Doctor?

05:30.000 --> 05:34.000
No, that's the undertaker. I give him all my business.

05:39.000 --> 05:42.000
Don't worry. Don't...

05:42.000 --> 05:44.000
Take it easy. You're a brave man.

05:44.000 --> 05:49.000
We've had enough of this silly chatter. I have an engagement with the lady in an hour.

05:49.000 --> 05:51.000
Let us proceed.

05:51.000 --> 05:53.000
I think I left something in the oven.

06:06.000 --> 06:08.000
What is he going to use?

06:08.000 --> 06:12.000
I don't know. He uses this all the time.

06:38.000 --> 06:40.000
Oh, no!

06:58.000 --> 07:01.000
Nothing happened.

07:01.000 --> 07:05.000
Oh, no!

07:05.000 --> 07:07.000
Olga!

07:10.000 --> 07:14.000
This way. Down and raise it.

07:15.000 --> 07:18.000
Raise this.

07:18.000 --> 07:20.000
Raise this.

07:20.000 --> 07:22.000
And this.

07:22.000 --> 07:24.000
And this.

07:24.000 --> 07:26.000
This must be...

07:26.000 --> 07:28.000
Now!

07:28.000 --> 07:30.000
Annie!

07:30.000 --> 07:53.000
Now take your sword and...

07:53.000 --> 08:03.000
Up! Up! Here, your sword. And your hat.

08:03.000 --> 08:07.000
That will teach you to insult my nose.

08:07.000 --> 08:10.000
Come, my Renault. We must be off.

08:10.000 --> 08:12.000
No, this way.

08:17.000 --> 08:19.000
I'm sorry.

08:19.000 --> 08:23.000
Quite all right, old man.

08:24.000 --> 08:30.000
Just the room of Lady Roxalt. For surely no such glow could flow but from the seat of heaven.

08:30.000 --> 08:36.000
Oh, Macaronio, with your words and my looks, surely we'll win.

08:36.000 --> 08:38.000
My fair lady.

08:38.000 --> 08:43.000
I shall secret myself behind this pillar and speak for thee.

08:43.000 --> 08:50.000
Cast a pebble at Lady Roxalt's window to fetch her hither, and then my voice shall do the rest.

08:56.000 --> 09:00.000
Who are thee? Who doth my yonder window break?

09:00.000 --> 09:03.000
Ay, my Renault. I have come to woo thee.

09:03.000 --> 09:10.000
Woo on, then. But be warned, none but the silken tongue shall win me.

09:10.000 --> 09:16.000
Then won you are. Oh, shining light of love. Oh, beautiful one.

09:16.000 --> 09:24.000
For thee, I would slay a thousand men, swim the Hellespont, climb Mount Olympus to fetch for thee the very head of Zeus.

09:24.000 --> 09:26.000
Will you marry me?

09:26.000 --> 09:33.000
Ay, yes. Ay, yes. I can say not but yes. Your dulcet tones have won me.

09:33.000 --> 09:39.000
Oh, Macaronio. You, with your words, you have won her for me.

09:39.000 --> 09:43.000
Wait. I shall come to thee.

09:43.000 --> 09:47.000
Marlon. I am ready.

09:47.000 --> 09:52.000
My life. My life.

09:53.000 --> 09:56.000
My voice. What has happened?

09:56.000 --> 10:03.000
He is so smitten with the love of thee that his voice has failed, O fairest flower that mine eyes have yet beheld.

10:03.000 --> 10:09.000
That is the voice I love.

10:09.000 --> 10:16.000
Well, it is faith. If I have lost, at least she has been won by my dear friend Macaronio.

10:16.000 --> 10:21.000
Macaroon, I am dying. Kiss me.

10:21.000 --> 10:28.000
The fairest flower in all of... The fairest...

10:51.000 --> 10:56.000
The fairest flower in all of...

11:21.000 --> 11:26.000
The fairest flower in all of...

